    "created_at": "2019-06-28T16:14:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-06-28T16:14:57Z",
    "body": "For what it's worth, today I found more attributes that have this behavior of mapping as dimension and reflecting as unsigned int: vspace and hspace on `<marquee>`, `<img>`, and `<object>`.  I'm guessing pretty much no one ever specifies them as percentages, though, because Firefox wasn't even treating them as dimension attributes...\r\n\r\nI agree that for video it's not clear that we can really do much.  If sites are using those attributes in calculations, changing the reflection would break them.  If sites are using percentage values in the attributes, changing the mapping would break them.  I guess we could do the latter if in practice no one uses percentage dimensions on `<video>`, or we could just leave the inconsistency and live with it...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
